From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:50:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] feat(embed): the review panel host apps embed, at
 /embed

The page a host app puts in an iframe so its
users review a doop canvas without ever going to doop: look at a frame,
pin comments, reply and resolve, request changes or approve, compare a
revision with the state the last verdict was given on.

- A second Vite entry (embed.html, src/embed/) with its own bundle: React,
  the frame runtime and its own files, about 270 KB of script and CSS over
  the wire against the editor's 2 MB. Plain CSS in doop's white system.
- Served at /embed only while DOOP_EMBED_HOSTS names a host, with
  frame-ancestors listing the host origins, no-store and no-referrer;
  /embed.html is a 404 so the file never goes out without those rules.
- The token comes in the URL fragment, is read once and wiped from the
  address, and is traded for the session with fetch (0011's exchange).
- Frames are drawn by the editor's own sandboxed iframe and runtime, so a
  comment is pinned on the element the runtime finds under the pointer
  (selector, element id, origin), exactly as the editor pins one.
- Request changes gives the verdict first and posts the pinned comment
  after it: pinning may stamp an element id, which moves the frame's
  version on, and the verdict belongs to the version that was looked at.
- Compare shows the frame beside the version filed with its last verdict
  (0010's history), at one scale, with the text runs that changed.
- postMessage to the host page's origin only: doop:ready, doop:open,
  doop:verdict (status, by, frameUpdatedAt, versionId), doop:comment,
  doop:need-token; from it, only doop:token and doop:open.

Checked end to end in a browser with a stand-in host app signing tokens
(perf/embed-e2e.mjs in the build repo): the panel opens a frame,
pins a comment on "Link works 7 days", requests changes (doop records the
verdict and files the version), shows the agent's revision as "Revised
since changes were requested", compares (Link works 7 days -> Link
expires Wed 19 Nov), approves; the host page hears every step; the
reviewer's own PATCH of the frame is refused (403). Tests:
embedPage.test.ts, embedChanges.test.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
